<title>USA: Code-Alarm rejects settlement offer.</title>
<headline>Code-Alarm rejects settlement offer.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON HEIGHTS, Mich. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Code-Alarm Inc said Monday it has rejected a $2 million pre-trial settlement offer in connection with a patent suit filed against Vista, Calif.-based Directed Electronics.</p>
<p>Code Alarm said it has sued the company for allegedly infringing its patent.</p>
<p>The offer was made in the pre-trial settlement conference in U.S. District Court for the Southern District of California, the company said. A jury trial on the matter is scheduled for July 8.</p>
<p>&quot;As always, we stand ready to settle if an equitable settlement is offered. However, Directed's most recent offer is wholly inadequate,&quot; Code-Alarm President and CEO Rand Mueller said in a statement.</p>
<p>Code-Alarm makes electronic vehicle security devices.</p>
</text>
